_meanings:
An affix added to nouns in the
 sense of ‘measuring as much as’, ‘as high or long, or broad as’, ‘reaching
 as far as’, as in {#UrumAtrI BittiH#}; {#paYcadaSayojanamAtramaDvAMnamaticakrAma#}
 <ls>K.</ls>; (in this sense the word may as well be considered to be {#mAtrA#}
 at the end of <ab>comp.</ab> <ab>q. v.</ab> below).

.²1 A measure, whether of length, breadth, height, size, space, distance
 or number; {#agre tizWata mAtraM me#} <ls>Bhāg. 6. 11. 5</ls>; usually at the
 end of comp, {%<ab>i. e.</ab>%} {#aNgulimAtram#} a ‘fingerʼs breadth’; {#kiMcinmAtraM#}
 {#gatvA#} ‘to some distance’; {#kroSamAtre#} ‘at the distance of a Krośa’,
 {#reKAmAtramapi#} ‘even the breadth of a line, as much as a line’; {#reKAmAtramapi#}
 {#kzuRRAdA manorvartmanaH param#} ({#na vyatIyuH#}) <ls>R. 1. 17</ls>; so {#kzaRamAtram#},
 {#nimizamAtram#} ‘the space of an instant’, {#SatamAtra#} ‘a hundred in
 number’; so {#gajamAtra#} ‘as high or big as an elephant’;

 {#tAlamAtra, yavamAtra#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 The full measure of anything, the whole or entire class of things,
 totality; {#jIvamAtram#} or {#prARimAtram#} ‘the entire class of living
 beings’; {#manuzyamAtro martyaH#} ‘every man is mortal’; {#vastumAtrapakzako'nupasaMhArI#}
 ({#hetuH#}) <ls>Tarka K.</ls>; {#mAnuzamAtraduzkaraM karmAnuzWitam#} <ls>Dk.</ls>
.²3 The simple measure of anything, the one thing and no more, often translatable
 by ‘mere’, ‘only’, ‘even’; {#jAtimAtreRa#} <ls>H. 1. 58</ls> ‘by mere caste’, {#wiwwiBamAtreRa#}
 {#samudro vyAkulIkftaH#} <ls n="H.">2. 149</ls> ‘by a mere wag-tail’, {#vAcAmAtreRa jApyase#}
 <ls>Ś. 2</ls> ‘merely by words’; so {#arTamAtram, saMmAnamAtram#} <ls>Pt. 1. 83</ls>; used
 with past participles {#mAtra#} may be translated by ‘as soon as’, ‘no
 sooner than’, ‘just’; {#vidDamAtraH#} <ls>R. 5. 51</ls> ‘as soon as pierced’; ‘when
 just pierced’; {#BuktamAtre#} ‘just after eating’; {#pravizwamAtra eva#}
 {#tatraBavati#} <ls>Ś. 3</ls> <ab>&c.</ab>
.²4 An element, elementary matter; {#ahaM payo jyotiraTAnilo naBo mAtrARi#}
 {#devA mana indriyARi#} <ls>Bhāg. 10. 59. 31</ls>.
